<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.12.1: Modeling Exponential Decay</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01461</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.12.1: Modeling Exponential Decay</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7689915b-0509-4579-b462-e4ff1bc8b97e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00001">Jada received a gift of $180. In the first week, she spent a third of the gift money. She continues spending a third of what is left each week thereafter.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00002">Which equation best represents the amount of gift money <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, in dollars, she has after <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math><emphasis> </emphasis>weeks?</para>
    <para id="para-00003"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00004"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00008"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00009">Explain your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <list id="list-00001">
      <item>Jada's initial gift is $180. Then, she spends a third <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> of the whole amount each week. This means that she has <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> left after each week because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> (the whole amount minus a third).</item>
      <item>When writing the equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> because that is the starting amount she was given. Then, because she spends <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> each week, that means only <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> is leftover. so, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>. The equation that results is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>180</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>23</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
    </list>
  
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content></document>